      "source": "330-carving.md#330-slide; 320-ground-contact.md#320-probe; ResearchData/telemetry/ice-pingpong-20260721-162212.jsonl",
      "note": "Pose offset slews toward -60*lean*min(1, speed*0.694444) engine units at 66.666664 units/s and feeds BOTH the render position and the contact probe base. Direction is out of the turn (166/167 high-lean retail frames, mean -34.6 cm against the centripetal direction). The rider tune byte scale measured 1.07 mean (p10 0.98, p90 1.11) on the Gari PAL pad trace, so the port carries 1.0. The offset-base probe is what lets a carve on concave terrain read a deeper contact error and build the response toward its 2A clamp; without it ice carve force stays pinned at the flat-ground neutral equilibrium."
    },
